# The versions the upgrade test (scripts/upgrade-check.mjs, the `upgrade` job in heavy.yml)
# moves a site FROM, one per line: a git ref, or npm:tinyzoo@<version> for the packages as
# published. A site made with that version's `tinyzoo init` is upgraded to the current code;
# the check fails when it cannot be.
#
# Before the first release the baseline is a commit, not a tag. Once releases exist the
# latest release tag (v0.2.0, or tinyzoo@0.2.0 as Changesets writes it) is added
# automatically: the script resolves the keyword `latest-tag`, so nothing is needed here.
# Keep an older line while sites may still be on it; remove it when that stops being true.

# First commit with snake_case table names (merge of the 0.2 table-name work). Earlier
# commits need the interactive rename documented in the changeset.
2506403

# The first release, as sites installed it: tinyzoo and @tinyzoo/client 0.2.0 from npm, the site
# made with `pnpm dlx tinyzoo@0.2.0 init`. 1.0's promise is that a 0.2 site gets to the current
# version by following docs/upgrading.md (an `npm:` line needs its release tag in the clone, for
# the lockfile).
npm:tinyzoo@0.2.0
